{"agent":"n3-kilo","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`launch_env` always maps the child key variable to that same name (`{ep.api_key_env: ep.api_key_env}`) whenever `api_key_env` is set, and `Prepared` / the opencode launch pass that map as `LaunchSpec.env` together with `secret_env`. `secret_env` still resolves “variable first, then key file” into the same child variable. `LaunchSpec.env` is defined as a live source-name lookup that refuses the launch when that name is missing. Given an endpoint whose key is only in the key file (`api_key_env` set, process environment unset, file readable), prepare succeeds with a real value in `secret_env`, then launch refuses because `env` demands the unset variable. Previously `env` was `{}` and only the resolved secret was passed, so the file-backed key ran. The same overlap also keeps a prepare-time snapshot in `secret_env` after the source variable is revoked, so the “refuse rather than run stale” behavior is not actually enforced by this change.","digest":"b206bcb69177aa0b","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/lanes/endpoint.py:launch_env","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/lanes/endpoint.py:launch_env"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":16763,"diff_sha":"615546d902978f5ea7a64e13d1ae1dc64bb2a8affcca17573460b97e1d661638","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B26c3e73d84","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":65.0,"excluded_bytes":1956160,"excluded_files":1,"excluded_paths":["tests/test_uc_surf_setup_ops_transcript.json"],"family":"xai","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"5ebb10e61d3b9b56","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B26c3e73d84.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261111T042305Z-fba2cde1.jsonl","reason":"","review_degraded":[{"at":1794370985.617999,"f